{{Rootnotes
| name = Swashbuckle
| desc = [[Root]] sources do not interrupt the ability if already dashing.
}}

{{Rootnotes
| name = Shield Crash
| desc = [[Root]] sources applied to Pangolier does not moves Pangolier forward upon cast.
}}

{{Debuffnotes
| name = Roll Up
| desc = The {{M|forced movement}} applied no longer affects the [[debuff immune]] enemy unit.
}}
{{Draftnotes
| name = Roll Up
| desc = Requires drafting {{Symbol|bonus shd}} {{A|Pangolier|Rolling Thunder}} to this ability.
}}

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Roll Up icon0}}
| desc = Pangolier curls into an immobile protective ball, gaining debuff immunity, 80% magic resistance, and allowing him to turn. Can be cast during Rolling Thunder to temporarily hit the brakes. Can cast Rolling Thunder and Shield Crash during Roll Up. If enemies attack Pangolier during this, he will roll away from the attacker, applying Rolling Thunder damage/stun if there are enemies in the way.
}}
* Grants the following bonuses while active:
** {{Symbol|a|Up}} {{Symbol|Affect|Self}} {{Symbol|Magic Resistance}}
*** Has {{Code|{{calc|1-(1-{{G|magic resistance}})*(1-v1)|v1={{#var:Roll Up value1}}|%}} + {{calc|(1-v1)*{{G|bonus magic resistance}}|v1={{#var:Roll Up value1}}|%}} × Σ[[Intelligence|Int]]}} {{M|magic resistance}} per stack.
** The {{M|turn rate}} is given as degrees per second, instead of radians per {{M|server tick}}.
*** Has a {{#expr:{{#explode:{{#var:Roll Up value2}}|°}}*{{G|deg to turn rate}}}}-{{M|turn rate}} ({{Code|{{#expr:{{#explode:{{#var:Roll Up value2}}|°}}*{{G|deg to rad}}}} [[Wikipedia:Radian|rad]]}}).

{{Debuffnotes
| name = Rolling Thunder
| desc = The {{M|forced movement}} applied no longer affects the [[debuff immune]] enemy unit.
}}
{{Rootnotes
| name = Rolling Thunder
| desc = [[Root]] sources cause Pangolier remains stationary until the {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} modifier duration ends.
}}

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Rolling Thunder icon0}}
| desc = Pangolier curls into a debuff immune ball with 80% magic resistance and rolls out. When rolling, he moves at an increased speed and can move through trees, but has a decreased ability to turn. Striking enemies knocks them back, inflicting damage proportional to his attack damage and stunning them when they land.<br><br>Colliding with walls or cliffs will cause a temporary pause while Pangolier reverses in direction.
}}
* {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
** Grants the following bonuses while active:
*** {{Symbol|a|Up}} {{Symbol|Affect|Self}} {{Symbol|Magic Resistance}}
**** Has {{Code|{{calc|1-(1-{{G|magic resistance}})*(1-v1)|v1={{#var:Rolling Thunder value2}}|%}} + {{calc|(1-v1)*{{G|bonus magic resistance}}|v1={{#var:Rolling Thunder value2}}|%}} × Σ[[Intelligence|Int]]}} {{M|magic resistance}} per stack.
** {{Symbol|Turn Rate}}
*** Turns for a max of 1 second per issued move order.
**** A single move order does not cause him to move in a circle around the {{Symbol|Target|Point}} point-targeted location.
**** Pangolier's final path and direction pre-move order corresponds to a vector from his position to the point-targeted location, which is parallel with the path.
*** The [[turn rate]] values is expressed in [[Wikipedia:Angle|θ]][[Wikipedia:Second|s]]<sup>-1</sup> within the ability in-game files.

* With {{M|unobstructed movement}} sources, only the edges of the map will cause Pangolier to roll back to the previous direction he came from.

{{Rootnotes
| name = Rolling Thunder
| desc = [[Root]] sources cause Pangolier remains stationary until the {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} modifier duration ends.
}}

