fields.value:
{{Rootnotes
| name = Shield Crash
| desc = [[Root]] sources applied to Pangolier does not moves Pangolier forward upon cast.
}}
{{Stealnotes
| name = Shield Crash
| desc = {{Symbol|bonus shd}} {{A|Pangolier|Swashbuckle}} applied is based on Pangolier's corresponding level when acquired.
}}
{{Draftnotes
| name = Shield Crash
| desc = {{Symbol|bonus shd}} Requires drafting {{A|Pangolier|Swashbuckle}} for its corresponding component to work.
}}

 * The ability effects are applied as follows:
*# {{Symbol|Caster|Leap}}
*#* Interrupts Pangolier's {{M|channeling}} abilities upon cast.
*#* Applies a {{M|disabling}} {{#var:Shield Crash value2}}-distance {{M|forced movement}} with a 250-height {{M|upward movement}}.
*#* Can jump over other units and {{M|impassable terrain}}.
*#** The jump length corresponds to the current terrain, jumping onto a higher or lower ground affects the jump duration, without affecting the jump distance.
*# {{cf|aghnotes}} [[File:Dota2 Pangolier Shield Crash agh Visualization.png|84px]] {{Symbol|Facing Angle|r}}
*#* Applies {{A|Pangolier|Swashbuckle}} of its corresponding level upon cast.
*#** Hence, the {{ValueColor||{{#var:Shield Crash type3 value2 agh}}|agh}} Swashbuckle slashes do not follow Pangolier's current location, but corresponds to Pangolier current [[File:Dota2 Letter-o.png|O|21px]] {{Symbol|Facing Angle|r}} [[facing angle]], and with [[File:Dota2 Letter-o.png|O|21px]] [[File:Dota2 Letter-q.png|Q|21px]] being the slash range and slash width.
*#*** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|OQ {{=}} OQ<nowiki>'</nowiki> {{=}} OQ<nowiki>''</nowiki> {{=}} OQ<nowiki>'''</nowiki>}}
*#** Swashbuckle cast this way neither cancels the {{Symbol|Gyroshell|shd}} {{Symbol|Gyroshell|ult}} Gyroshell form nor causes him to {{M|cannot act}}.
*#** Works independently of Swashbuckle's {{M|cooldown}}, and does not cost {{M|mana}}.
*#** Multiple Swashbuckle area-of-effect stacks.
*# {{Symbol|Projectile|Impact}}
*#* Applies the {{M|physical}} {{M|spell damage}}
*# {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{A|Pangolier|Lucky Shot}}
*# {{Symbol|bonus db-all}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{to}} {{Code|pangolier_shield_crash_buff}}
*#* Requires damaging one enemy hero for this ability component to take effect.
*#** Considers {{M|clones}} and the {{H|Spirit Bear}} as enemy heroes, {{M|illusions}} and other {{M|creep-heroes}} as creeps.
*#* Reapplying the buff on Pangolier refreshes the buff duration.

* {{Symbol|Projectile|Roll}}
** The ability additionally has the following properties while in {{Symbol|Gyroshell|shd}} {{Symbol|Gyroshell|ult}} Gyroshell forms:
*** Pangolier is moved {{Symbol|Upward Movement}} vertically and not {{Symbol|Forced Movement}} horizontally.
*** Both the vertical and horizontal movement stack with each other, and does not interfere with abilities that moves Pangolier either on the x-axis or the y-axis.
*** When cast during {{A|Pangolier|Rolling Thunder}}:
**** {{Symbol|Caster|Leap}}
***** Jumps in an arc with a max {{#var:Shield Crash type2 value2}}-height with the set roll speed.
***** When the Rolling Thunder expires during the Shield Crash jump, Rolling Thunder's duration is extended based on the Shield Crash jump duration, keeping the roll speed until landing.
***** However, the roll speed is lost upon the {{A|Pangolier|Stop Rolling}} {{M|sub-ability}} cast, and Pangolier falls straight down in this situation.
*** {{cf|shdnotes}} When cast during {{A|Pangolier|Roll Up}}:
**** {{Symbol|Upward Movement}}
***** Jumps at {{ValueColor||{{#var:Shield Crash type4 value1 shd}}|shd}}-height upon cast and does not jumps in an arc.
***** Other aformentioned {{A|Pangolier|Rolling Thunder}} ability notes apply.

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Shield Crash icon0}}
| desc = Pangolier jumps in the air and slams back to the ground in front of his current position damaging all enemies in a radius. Pangolier gains an all damage barrier for a short time if Shield Crash hits an enemy hero.<br><br>Forward movement is maintained if Shield Crash is used while Rolling Thunder is active, and allows Rolling Thunder to clear walls or cliffs.
}}
{{Barriercard}}

* {{Symbol|fx|v}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
** The five circling shields ability effect around Pangolier has 3 different states:
*** When {{Code|< 2}} enemy heroes hit, the shields are small and have no extra effects.
*** When {{Code|{{=}} 3}} enemy heroes hit, the shields are larger and gain a light yellow flame-like effect.
*** When {{Code|> 4}} enemy heros hit, the yellow flame is more intense.

